From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: llama: mixed embedding batches and device-resident MTP drafting

- llama_batch.embd_input: rows that carry both a token id and an embedding
  (zero for text tokens; audio embeddings with token -1) in one batch.
  embd_input_device lets the graph read rows already staged on the device.
- MTP hidden states can stay on the device (llama_set_embeddings_nextn_device,
  batch.embd_device), and draft steps chain on the device
  (llama_set_mtp_chain): argmax ids and hidden rows are written back in place,
  with no host round trip between drafts.
- The draft context accepts position gaps for deferred catch-up and can wait on
  another context's event (llama_set_input_wait_event).
- common/speculative's MTP driver uses these paths when the target context has
  batched serving. Its queued row moves run as one gather and one scatter per
  (source, destination) pair, and common_speculative_copy_state copies a
  sequence's drafter state on the device.

Upstream: not planned in this form; device-resident drafting may be proposed
alongside upstream's MTP work.

